=== ARM K — basin sampling of the survey on 10-rule-in-pyproject (35B): is the J3 miss a basin or a rate? (pre-registered 2026-09-13 04:20 UTC, before launch)
Trigger: arm J cell J-SURVEY-35B-10 passed 1/3 (turns 16/17/17) against J-NOSURVEY-35B-10 3/3 (9/9/9) — a J3 miss by the letter, which reopens the survey default. Pinned N=3 on a deterministic pod is one sample of one basin (ADR-0160, rb-10849); the outcome question needs sampled basins.
Mechanism seen in J (dumps, names only): with the survey the 35B skips the listing, reads slug.py first and pyproject.toml fourth; without it, three list_dir calls then pyproject.toml first. No run in any arm (J, NT) ran the lint; the failing runs' verifier tail is ruff's docstring-section rule from pyproject [tool.ruff] ("Add blank line after Raises").
Build: main@a383da8 (#429, verify_auto present but OFF in both arms) src 8ea8bacece34 on zc-01 (/opt/zak-code-bench), swapped in after arm J ended.
Cells: K-{NOSURVEY,SURVEY}-35B-10, --no-pin (fresh mkdtemp workspace per run), temperature 0, stable identity, dumps on; N=6 per arm, interleaved in threes: NOSURVEY×3, SURVEY×3, NOSURVEY×3, SURVEY×3 (b1, b2).
Measures: pass RATE per arm; turns; wall medians; distinct output states; opening listing calls; whether pyproject.toml is the first read; lint runs (expected 0).
Rules:
 K1: SURVEY pass rate ≤ NOSURVEY − 2 (of 6) → the survey costs outcomes on this task: flip context_workspace_survey back to default OFF (ADR-0164's refusal restored), keep opt-in; the durable fix is a check the model cannot skip (L4: auto-derived lint/verify from Makefile/pyproject), to be measured next.
 K2: |SURVEY − NOSURVEY| ≤ 1 → a basin, not a rate: the default stays ON; record the J3 miss as a pinned-basin artifact beside arm G's 6/6 vs 5/6.
 K3: SURVEY ≥ NOSURVEY + 2 → surprising; record, no claim without replication.
 K4 (descriptive): reading order and listing calls per arm; turns medians.
Predictions: SURVEY 3–4/6, NOSURVEY 5–6/6 → K1 at the boundary; the honest prior is a coin, so the letter decides.
Cost: 12 runs × 190–470 s ≈ 45–70 min of pod time.
